<title>LATVIA: PM SHKELE SEES 5 PCT GDP GROWTH IN 1998.</title>
<headline>PM SHKELE SEES 5 PCT GDP GROWTH IN 1998.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvian Prime Minister Andris Shkele believes the government will reach its target of five percent growth in Gross Domestic Product (GDP) from next year.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope for 1998 we will be able to reach it and even be over it,&quot; Shkele told Reuters in an interview on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
